 in 1990, DGC's distribution moved to MCA on 1 January 1991 for the US, and to BMG on 1 April 1991 outside the US. \r\n\r\nWound down in the late 1990s as most of its artists were absorbed by either [l=Geffen Records] or [l=Interscope Records] when the [l=Universal Music Group] purchased [l=PolyGram] in 1999 and Geffen became part of Interscope Records.\r\n\r\nHowever, [l=DGC Records] continued with [a=Beck] and [a=Sonic Youth] as its only artists until 2003. In 2007, it was relaunched as a direct subsidiary of [l=Interscope Geffen A&M] Records. In September 2021, DGC was once again permanently merged into Geffen Records, transferring the remains of its roster to either Geffen or Interscope.\r\n\r\n[u]Counterfeit / unofficial releases that pretend to be issued under this label must use [l230564] instead[/u].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:86487","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":265932,"name":"The David Geffen Company"},"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/86487-DGC","type":"label","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DGC_Records"]}},"/api/discogs/release/11341576":{"cached":true,"release":{"artists":[{"id":null,"name":"Moka Only"}],"formats":[],"genres":["Hip Hop"],"id":"11341576","images":[],"labels":[{"catno":"URBNET1227LP","id":71029,"name":"Urbnet Records"}],"styles":["Jazzy Hip-Hop"],"title":"Concert For One","tracklist":["Concert Intro","Hi","UnU","Featuring Drake","Demoland","Replay","Just Some Vibes","Are You Happy Now","Snapshot","Right There","Egg Interlude","Not A Thing","I May","Green Bridge Interlude","Real Simple Real Mellow","Old Quirks Old Places","Real Late","Grinkle Jazz","The Stars","What Zone Now"],"uri":"https://www.discogs.com/release/11341576","videos":[],"year":2017}},"/api/discogs/release/115228":{"cached":true,"release":{"artists":[{"id":null,"name":"So Solid Crew"}],"formats":[],"genres":["Electronic"],"id":"115228","images":[],"labels":[{"catno":"ISOM 27CD","id":2074,"name":"Independ